 "capsule": "Burma across this 1820–1990 span covers the final decades of the Konbaung dynasty, which fought three wars against British forces (1824–26, 1852, 1885) culminating in full annexation as a province of British India in 1886. Independence came in 1948 under U Nu, followed by Ne Win's 1962 coup and single-party 'Burmese Way to Socialism' military rule, which held until the 1988 pro-democracy uprising was crushed and the State Law and Order Restoration Council seized power. The country was officially renamed the Union of Myanmar in 1989, the distinct successor entity that shares this Wikidata identifier.",
